        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d433336d-bfba-5152-aa21-1f1c9fe690e5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Gould Shaw\n- Organizations: Union Army, 54th Massachusetts Infantry Regiment\n- Events: U.S. Civil War, Emancipation Proclamation\n- Concepts: abolitionism, equal pay\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Gould Shaw was born on October 10, 1837, into a prominent abolitionist family.\n- During the U.S. Civil War, Robert Gould Shaw was an American soldier in the Union Army.\n- The Emancipation Proclamation authorized the 54th Massachusetts Infantry Regiment.\n- The 54th Massachusetts Infantry Regiment was the first African-American regiment organized in the northern states during the Civil War.\n- The 54th Massachusetts Infantry Regiment consisted of African-American enlisted men commanded by white officers.\n- Robert Gould Shaw accepted command of the 54th Massachusetts Infantry Regiment, the first all-black regiment in the Northeast.\n- Robert Gould Shaw encouraged the men of the 54th Massachusetts Infantry Regiment to refuse their pay until it matched the wages of white troops.\n- Robert Gould Shaw died on July 18, 1863.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "0be690aa-86dd-52b8-af1e-05342ec6287c",
        "text": "Page: Robert Gould Shaw. Sentence: Robert Gould Shaw (October 10, 1837 – July 18, 1863) was an American soldier in the Union Army during the U.S. Civil War.\nPage: Robert Gould Shaw. Sentence: Born into a prominent abolitionist family, he accepted command of the first all-black regiment (54th Massachusetts) in the Northeast and encouraged the men to refuse their pay until it was equal to the white troops’ wage.\nPage: 54th Massachusetts Infantry Regiment. Sentence: The unit was the first African-American regiment organized in the northern states during the Civil War.\nPage: 54th Massachusetts Infantry Regiment. Sentence: Authorized by the Emancipation Proclamation, the regiment consisted of African-American enlisted men commanded by white officers.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
